 culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["National Health Investors, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.5B market cap on $376M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $57M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 50% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.496612790755113},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired 